source_proof = "Seven collected tests map the finding and check one chain-125 BFT paxd network, embedded block-proposing kernel, api1 through api14 root HTTPS JSON-RPC, parsed chain probe JSON, scoped hosted px_ contract, transaction acceptance/forwarding, WAL release before receipt publication, submitted/receipted/committed rungs, authenticated commitment guidance, both diagrams, the complete thirteen-entry merge address table, upgrade-gated retired custody/checkpoint executors, archive-only formats and paxd startup guidance. Production Go sources and the hosted OpenRPC JSON are read directly in-process."
review_only = "Native Go/C/Rust builds, execution of transactions, cryptographic verification, WAL restart/recovery, live endpoints and BFT consensus are not executed. Static source assertions qualify documentation connections, not runtime correctness or deployment. No production interface or stateful component changes, so interface-driving and restart tests do not apply to this doc-drift finding."
baseline = "Initial git status/diff showed only runner-prepared .cgignore and spec task bookkeeping; neither scoped file existed, gate.json recorded zero builds and verifies, and no gates.jsonl existed. The pre-change verify was not run: the explicit implementation-first order and exclusive hf-done gate supersede the older baseline instruction in step 5. No pre-change test failure is claimed."
